            <div xml:id="d278">

                <pb facs="0322" n="308" sameAs="frus:frus1943v06/pg308"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">816.24/705</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chief of the Division of the American
                        Republics</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bonsal</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Assistant Chief of the Division</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Cabot</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>], <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-07-09">July 9, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Cabot</hi>: Commander Parker spoke to me this
                    morning about the interest of the Salvadoran Military Attaché, whose name, I
                    believe, is Baroń, in obtaining 1,000 submachine guns. May I have your views <pb
                        facs="0323" n="309" xml:id="pg309"/> on this? It seems to me to be a rather
                    considerable order of an article which has played a sinister role in Central
                    America.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Philip W. Bonsal</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
